          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What is a urinary tract infection, and why are they more common in women?",
          "answer": "A urinary tract infection (UTI) is a bacterial infection of the urinary system. Most UTIs affect the bladder and urethra, which is called a lower tract infection or cystitis. If the infection reaches the kidney, it's called pyelonephritis, an upper tract infection, which is more serious. The bacterium *Escherichia coli* is the cause of most UTIs. (Source: condition-urinary-tract-infection)\n\nThe provided information does not explain why urinary tract infections are more common in women.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
